Three routes for the PM

Route A: the v2 route, then CI on policy v2
- Facts: the v2 debt is smaller than the v1 debt: additions=248 against 332, removals=16, renames=161. The v2 baselines date to 2026-08-19.
- The reconcile v2 preview is a no-op write of the same four files. It does not add the 248 findings.
- To make v2 clean, the accepted manifest needs baselineAdditions for the 248 findings (owner and rationale review metadata in each baseline entry), all review roles, and the owner binding with the owner receipt at measure/tracks/durable_job_worker_platform_20260713/owner-receipt.json. The manifest holds 0 reviews and 0 baselineAdditions now.
- No production command builds those manifest additions. buildAnalyzerReconciliationManifest is exported (reconciliation-manifest-builder.ts:510) and has no caller outside its test.
- CI change: .github/workflows/ci.yml:157 must become `pnpm architecture:check --policy v2 --skip-input-snapshot-pin`.
- Cost: new builder work, a full review set, and an owner receipt. It is the durable route but not a short one.

Route B: a code change that allows an acknowledged v1 baseline update
- Facts: writeArchitectureBaselines refuses the protected v1 baselines (baseline-update.ts:246-252).
- What breaks: V1_ARTIFACT_BINDINGS fixed accepted hashes (v1-validation.ts:33+), validateV1ArtifactFamilySync (v1-validation.ts:70+), the fixed V1_MANIFEST_SHA256 (policy-selection.ts:52-53), and the v2 manifest field v1ManifestSha256. policy-selection.ts:58-64 validates the v1 family for every policy, so both policies fail until the fixed hashes change.
- The v2 manifest also binds the v1 manifest hash, so a changed v1 family needs a v2 manifest update and re-acceptance.
- The v1 update accepts new debt only with --owner and --rationale (baseline-update.ts:35-38 and :129). The 332 additions need both.
- The v2 branch of baseline-update stays blocked: "Policy v2 baseline writes require the complete four-file reconciliation transaction" (baseline-update.ts:325-330).

Route C: keep CI red on the debt step until a remediation track and a later route
- Facts: the input pin is fixed. The CI step at .github/workflows/ci.yml:157 still exits 1 on v1 debt.
- The drift sits in other tracks' files (primary-advantage 144, accounts 50, marketing 18, sales 13, codecamp 11, reading 11). A remediation track has the most room to reduce it.
- Cost: the architecture job stays red. The other CI steps and the guards still run. A later route (A or B) lands after remediation.

Default of this role: route C for task 1.4 now, with route A opened as a separate task. Reasons: route C changes no contract and no protected artifact. Route A is the durable fix but needs an owner receipt, a full review set, and a manifest builder that does not exist outside its test. Route B breaks the protected v1 family and forces a v2 re-acceptance.

